/**
 * GALLBLADDER CANCER: LIVING WITH IT, CARE AND DECISIONS (UK and NHS focus). Facts checked 2026-09-24.
 *
 * The patient side of the gallbladder cancer record: three decision rows the decisions page turns into
 * sections (jaundice: stent or bypass; HER2 and genomic testing; a trial or standard treatment), the
 * hand-written question set the appointment sheet, prep pack and decision pages read (exported as
 * `gallbladderQuestions`, wired in src/data/questions.ts), and glossary records for the symptoms and the
 * practical side (jaundice and itch, stent problems, cholangitis, pain, weight loss and fat digestion,
 * fatigue, eating after gallbladder removal, when to seek urgent help, emotional support, carers).
 *
 * Every medical statement points at an NHS, Macmillan, Cancer Research UK, AMMF, Marie Curie or Maggie's
 * page, a NICE appraisal, the ESMO patient guide or a paper found through Europe PMC. Nothing here is
 * advice; the pages say so the way the site's other living-with material does. UK spelling, plain English.
 *
 * The cancer record itself (`gallbladder`, src/data/spikes/nci-rare-other.ts) is owned by the cancer pass;
 * if that record is renamed, change GALLBLADDER_CANCER_ID and the questions key together.
 */
